# DES BOP Console — Cursor AI Rules

## Adding a new screen or program — ALL FIVE STEPS ARE MANDATORY

A screen is incomplete until validate-structure.sh passes with zero errors.
Do not mark any task done until you have completed every step below.

### Step 1 — Screen Registry (lib/screen-registry.ts)
- Add the route: `'/console/seg/name': { id: 'XX000', title: '...', mod: 'MOD' }`
- Screen ID format: two-letter module prefix + 3-digit number (e.g. DEV001, INT002)
- Add module color to MOD_COLORS if the module prefix is new

### Step 2 — Navigation (components/Shell.tsx)
- Add nav item: `{ label: tn('keyName'), href: '/console/seg/name' }`
- Add group: `{ label: tg('groupKey'), ... }`
- NEVER use hardcoded strings. Always tn() for nav items, tg() for group labels.

### Step 3 — Translations (messages/nl.json, en.json, de.json, fr.json, tr.json)
Update ALL FIVE files. Each needs:
- `"nav": { "keyName": "translated label" }`
- `"groups": { "groupKey": "translated group name" }`
- `"screens": { "XX000": "translated screen name" }`

### Step 4 — Middleware (middleware.ts)
- Add to SEG_TO_MODULE: `seg: 'MOD'`
- Add MOD to ROLE_MODULES for every role that should access it

### Step 5 — Validate
```bash
bash scripts/validate-structure.sh
```
Fix all reported errors before running rebuild.sh.

## Hard rules
- Never hardcode strings in Shell.tsx nav labels
- Never create page.tsx without a screen-registry entry
- Never skip any of the 5 language files
- Never skip middleware.ts when adding a new path segment
- Run validate-structure.sh before every build

## Key files
- lib/screen-registry.ts — screen ID registry
- components/Shell.tsx — sidebar nav (i18n keys only)
- messages/{nl,en,de,fr,tr}.json — translations
- middleware.ts — RBAC (SEG_TO_MODULE + ROLE_MODULES)
- scripts/validate-structure.sh — structural integrity check
- rebuild.sh — build + deploy (calls validator automatically)
